    {
      "id": "842dbb67-577a-4c7e-b645-4f8e1dc8a84f",
      "name": "Sticky - sticky-main",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2240,
        2160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#EBED78",
        "width": 650,
        "height": 836,
        "content": "## **AI Document Processing Agent**\n\n**Who it's for:** Anyone who wants invoices, resumes, contracts, or applications automatically read, validated, and filed without manual data entry.\n\n**What it does:** Accepts a document by form upload or email attachment, uses AI to detect the type and extract structured fields, flags anything uncertain for human review, and files everything into the right Airtable table.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Upload a PDF via the form, or send it as a Gmail attachment\n2. Extracts the PDF text and normalizes it (source, submitter, raw text)\n3. Claude detects the document type and extracts the relevant fields\n4. Low-confidence or incomplete results go to Slack + an Airtable review queue\n5. Everything else is filed into its matching Airtable table (Invoice/Resume/Contract/Application)\n6. A Slack notification confirms successful processing\n\n**How to set up**\n☐ Connect Gmail (for the email intake path)\n☐ Add an Anthropic API credential (generic header auth)\n☐ Connect Airtable and create 5 tables: Invoices, Resumes, Contracts, Applications, Needs Review\n☐ Connect Slack and set your review + general channel IDs\n\n**CUSTOMIZATION**\n- Add more document types to the AI prompt and the Switch node\n- Adjust the confidence threshold for manual review (default: 0.6)\n- Add a Loop node if emails may contain multiple attachments"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "eaaeb0e9-1ec5-47d5-bce8-b80d46d1e131",
      "name": "Sticky - sticky-sec",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2912,
        2384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1142,
        "height": 482,
        "content": "**1. Intake (Form or Email)**\nAccepts a document two ways: a web form upload, or a Gmail attachment poller. Both paths extract the PDF text and normalize it into the same shape.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0b978410-2733-498e-8911-6fe4af36f772",
      "name": "Sticky - sticky-sec1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4768,
        1952
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1142,
        "height": 978,
        "content": "**3. Review & Route**\nLow-confidence or incomplete extractions go to Slack + Airtable for manual review. Everything else is routed by document type into its own Airtable table, then a success notification is sent."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
